<title>USA: U.S. banks free reserves $910 mln July 16 two wks.</title>
<headline>U.S. banks free reserves $910 mln July 16 two wks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $910 million per day in the two weeks ended July 16, versus revised free reserves of $573 million in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $299 million versus $300 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
